# The White Oak — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. Never commit `.env.local`.
# See `.gitignore` — `.env*` is excluded (with an explicit exception for this file).
#
# For Vercel deployments, set the same variable names with environment-specific
# VALUES under Project → Settings → Environment Variables, scoped to
# Production / Preview / Development. See:
#   docs/how-to-guides/configure-propertybase-env.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public site URL (drives absolute URLs for OG image, canonical link, etc.)
#
# Priority order in app/layout.tsx:
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL  — set this once you cut DNS to the custom domain
#   2. VERCEL_URL            — auto-injected by Vercel per deploy; current fallback
#   3. http://localhost:3000 — dev fallback
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://thewhiteoakhouston.com

# =============================================================================
# Propertybase / Salesforce
#
# `/api/subscribe` will POST a pba__Request__c (Inquiry) to the Salesforce
# REST API. The same code targets sandbox or production depending on which
# env values are loaded — no branching in code.
#
# Per-environment values (set differently in each Vercel environment):
#   Local dev (.env.local)  → sandbox
#   Vercel Preview          → sandbox
#   Vercel Development      → sandbox  (only matters when running `vercel dev`)
#   Vercel Production       → production
#
# Both Salesforce orgs require their own Connected App — the consumer key
# from the sandbox app will NOT authenticate against production and
# vice-versa.
#
# Note: RecordTypeId, picklist values, and other schema-level constants are
# replicated between Nan's sandbox and production orgs, so they stay
# hardcoded in lib/propertybase-mapping.ts (INQUIRY_DEFAULTS). The only
# values that need env-scoping are the instance URL + auth credentials.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Salesforce instance (My Domain) — different per org
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sandbox example:
#   PROPERTYBASE_INSTANCE_URL=https://my-nanproperties--partialbox.sandbox.my.salesforce.com
# Production:
#   PROPERTYBASE_INSTANCE_URL=https://my-nanproperties.my.salesforce.com
PROPERTYBASE_INSTANCE_URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auth credentials (TBD — depends on which auth flow we pick)
#
# Likely candidates:
#   - OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials Flow (server-to-server, no per-user OAuth)
#       → needs PROPERTYBASE_CLIENT_ID + PROPERTYBASE_CLIENT_SECRET
        → aka Consumer Key and Consumer Secret
#   - JWT Bearer Flow (also server-to-server)
#       → needs PROPERTYBASE_CLIENT_ID + PROPERTYBASE_USERNAME + RSA private key
#   - Long-lived OAuth access token (simplest, less secure)
#       → needs PROPERTYBASE_ACCESS_TOKEN
#
# Auth approach: OAuth 2.0 Client Credentials Flow (decided). Set both:
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPERTYBASE_CLIENT_ID=
PROPERTYBASE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# =============================================================================
# Lead emails (Resend)
#
# /api/subscribe sends two emails to a human inbox (see lib/lead-fallback.ts):
#   1. A new-lead notification on every successful submission.
#   2. A lost-lead fallback when Propertybase is unreachable, so no lead is lost.
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY     — from https://resend.com (per-account; same key works
#                        across environments)
#   LEAD_FALLBACK_TO   — recipient(s) for both emails. Comma-separated to add
#                        teammates, e.g. "tony@nan...,mary@nan...".
#   LEAD_FALLBACK_FROM — sender; MUST be on a Resend-verified domain. For local
#                        testing you can use onboarding@resend.dev (only
#                        delivers to your own Resend signup email). For prod,
#                        verify a domain and use e.g. leads@thewhiteoakhouston.com.
# =============================================================================
RESEND_API_KEY=
LEAD_FALLBACK_TO=
LEAD_FALLBACK_FROM=
